---
import { repositoryUrl, downloadSize } from '../config/product';
---

<section class="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <h2 id="features-title" class="features-title">Everything else you’d expect, and nothing you don’t.</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <h3>Lightweight by design</h3>
      <p>A native reader for Windows and Android. The Windows app is a {downloadSize} download built with Rust that opens quickly and stays out of the way.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Local and offline</h3>
      <p>Your books, notes and reading progress stay on your device. No account. Nothing to upload.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Four reading themes</h3>
      <p>Default, Soft, Clear or Compact, in light or dark. Every font is bundled, so nothing is downloaded.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Shelves for your books</h3>
      <p>Group books into your own shelves, then filter and sort. Favourites and Continue Reading are always close.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Find in the book</h3>
      <p>Search inside PDF, EPUB and HTML with Ctrl+F and jump straight to each match.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Source-available</h3>
      <p>See how your reader works. The code is <a href={repositoryUrl}>on GitHub</a>.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
